notes: 'M2231 explicitly enumerates 6 g source-labelled K2HPO4·7H2O and 1 L deionized
  water for the stock, dosed at 5 ml into Allen medium. This resolves the stock-strength
  versus receiving-volume confusion, but does not verify that the literal seven-water
  compound is chemically correct. Its component stays UNMAPPED; original unqualified
  component case remains chemically held. Raw case labels remain only in evidence
  and case-bound proposal links, not globally resolving synonyms. No occurrence count
  transfer, source-hold release or receiving-medium dose correction is implied. Issue
  1227 source-relative completeness: M2231 paragraph 9 enumerates literal K2HPO4·7H2O,
  6 g, and deionized water, 1 L. The receiving recipe doses 5 ml of that stock. Both
  printed inputs are retained; chemical validity of seven waters remains unresolved.
  Completeness describes the literal printed input list only; it does not approve
  a disputed chemical identity, a final volume or source membership transfer.'
